<description>&lt;p&gt;The Colombian government has called in U.S. intelligence and cut a deal with Venezuela to free two ELN hostages, while ELN and FARC dissident groups continue fighting for control, leaving civilians under siege. A Trump-backed right-wing lawyer has apparently won the presidential election, and the new administration faces a wave of violence that includes more than 45 social leaders killed in the first 100 days of President De la Espriella, arrests of high-profile criminals, and accusations that six individuals are part of a Colombian-Russian drug-trafficking network linked to FARC dissidents. An earthquake in southwestern Colombia has caused over 224 deaths and ongoing rescue operations. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMifEFVX3lxTE9WdXpzT0V2MllGaGJ4eTl5dTB4bEhnNTZhMjRsRlRVZ1ozVjJOVWI4SmRYQTBOOFNOeElaMFd0Z0MxZUc2QXd0eE1zT2MxQUhYRU5KX2NkNzZfNlduOVowR1FQUmpJeUU1UzluZ25qbEl6UkFDa2ZGSXpQUlE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Kansas City Star&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Global Witness&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxPUElMUmoxLVdnWUdNZzNMQUxtWWlJdHZNX3lkWUdobU5ORm9zbGhxblZodFFFT3c5aFU1d0RxZjlwU2tKbnZneXlxX3ZvS1JxWU1lTVNqVDRDcGZMbGNfSE9LTThobXAxdkJQVG9zaFpTQzlfUzhacjl6ZWNOM3FCSXRwZ3N3WnoyNzh3TDlMTXp5bmJnM3VkOHkwdVJEeDY2V21OSXo4RzAtWm55cmJ2Qg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latin Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiekFVX3lxTE9pdWViVDJZcFNCY3BzbnY5eWNUNWp4MDBYWTNTTnZWdGNqbGhma2xoRkhYTmUtWVJIVVZqN1I3U05IUjN0WE5hb19YN1lHdHo5NkdNTTVyRVQ0SW9rQ2hPV3U5ZzEwaUZUYnV5Tm40ZGlrT1dVM0FFZmZ3?oc=5&quot;&gt;ColombiaOne.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articl